From bfe60e913916faaa04500881e81a1d191ca7fa2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben <60955077+tencur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:12:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] vesuvius.predict TTA: read a direction's sign convention
 from its training losses

The shipped nearest_component_3d.yaml trains the direction with
SignInvariantCosineLoss (ChannelSelectLoss on all but the last channel)
and the trailing distance with SmoothL1Loss. The TTA transformed that
direction as a signed vector, so a network that reports the axis with the
same sign in every mirrored frame, which the loss allows, averaged to
(0, 0, 0, d) under default mirroring where main kept (1, 0, 0, d).

A vector head is now an axis when every loss configured on its direction
channels is SignInvariantCosineLoss (directly, or as the base of a
ChannelSelectLoss that does not select only the last channel). Any other
loss there (CosineSimilarityLoss, NormalSmoothnessLoss, a regression loss)
can supervise the orientation, so the head stays signed and is never
flipped, also when it is combined with a sign-invariant loss. Without a
configured direction loss, inplane_direction stays an axis and the other
vector heads stay signed. The nearest_component distance stays a scalar
average.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
