From 433dd618a9474eadc8b1296d510b66e9b33d7c46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben <60955077+tencur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:15:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] vesuvius.predict: write multiclass chunks of a single
 nonzero class

With --mode multiclass --threshold only the argmax is written. Once the
auxiliary heads are left out of the class selection, a chunk can hold
class 1 in every voxel; the finalizer skipped any chunk whose bytes were
all equal, so it read back as the fill value, class 0. That happened in
the in-memory blend, in finalize_outputs and in blend_and_finalize, which
share apply_finalization (segmentation-only outputs had the same problem
on main).

A finalized chunk is now skipped only when every byte equals the fill
value 0. test_homogeneous_chunk_is_still_skipped asserted the old
behaviour with a uniform class 2 chunk; it now checks a class 0 chunk,
and a new test checks that a uniform class 2 chunk is written. The
end-to-end test also runs finalize_outputs with --delete_intermediates,
which removes the logits only after every chunk has been written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
